<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"
     xmlns:gcse="http://www.google.com/cse"
     xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron"
     xmlns:xh="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
   <teiHeader>
      <fileDesc>
         <titleStmt>
            <title>Schema and Documentation for <title level="m">LWTA</title> project</title>
            <author>Martin Holmes</author>
         </titleStmt>
         <publicationStmt>
            <p>Free for any purpose</p>
         </publicationStmt>
         <sourceDesc>
            <p>Created to provide a simplified, constrained RNG and Schematron schema for authoring
               and editing the LWTA site in Oxygen, along with documentation.</p>
         </sourceDesc>
      </fileDesc>
   </teiHeader>
   <text>
      <front xml:id="frontMatter">
         <titlePage>
            <docTitle>
               <titlePart type="main">LWTA Renewed Project</titlePart>
               <titlePart type="sub">Manual for Author, Editors and Coders</titlePart>
            </docTitle>
            <docAuthor>Martin Holmes</docAuthor>
            <docDate>2026</docDate>
         </titlePage>
         <p>This collection of pages provides documentation and encoding examples for 
            the renewed version of the LWTA website. </p>
         <divGen type="toc"/>
      </front>
      <body>
         <div xml:id="projectHistory">
            <head>Project history</head>
            <p>[TODO]</p>
         </div>
         <div xml:id="requirements">
            <head>Requirements</head>
            <p>To <emph>edit</emph> material for LWTA, you will need to be using a 
            computer with the following software:</p>
            <list>
               <item>The <ref target="#git">Git</ref> client (to check 
                  materials out of and back into the repository)</item>
               <item>The 
                  <ref target="https://www.oxygenxml.com/download.html">Oxygen XML Editor</ref>. 
                  It it technically possible to edit the 
                  materials in any text editor, but the code will not be checked
                  or constrained, and you will not have a lot of the editing help
                  provided by the Oxygen editor, so the results will most likely be
                  invalid and may break the website.
               </item>
               <item>A recent install of Java.</item>
               <item>Apache Ant and ant-contrib.</item>
               <item>Dart Sass.</item>
            </list>
         </div>
         <div xml:id="projectMaterials">
            <head>Project materials and organization</head>
         </div>
         <div xml:id="buildProcess">
            <head>The build process</head>
            <p>The organization of the repository is designed to keep the editing process
               as simple as possible, by removing all site-level global features such as 
               menus and banners from the text which is actually being authored/edited. That
               means that a build process must be performed to produce the actual site which 
               is uploaded to the server. This section documents the build process.</p>
            <p>In order to run the full build process, you will need the following software
               to be installed on your computer:
               <list>
                  <item>Java (preferably version 1.8 or above)</item>
                  <item>
                     <ref target="https://ant.apache.org/">Apache Ant</ref> (current version)</item>
                  <item>
                     <ref target="https://sourceforge.net/projects/ant-contrib/">ant-contrib</ref> (current version)</item>
                  <!--<item>
                     <ref target="https://www.python.org/downloads/">Python 3</ref>
                  </item>-->
                  <item>
                     <ref target="https://sass-lang.com/install">Dart Sass</ref>
                  </item>
                  <item>
                     <ref target="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rsync">rsync</ref>
                  </item>
               </list>
            </p>
            <p>In the root folder is a file called <ident>build.xml</ident>, which is the 
               controller for the entire build process. It is a script file for the 
               <ref target="http://ant.apache.org/">Apache Ant</ref> build tool. To see 
               the full details of the build process, you can read that file, or just 
               open a terminal in the project root and type:                 
            </p>
            <p>
               <eg>ant -projecthelp</eg>
            </p>
            
         </div>
         <!--<div xml:id="codeTemplates">
            <head>Oxygen code templates (keyboard shortcuts)</head>
            <p>A range of convenient keyboard shortcuts are defined in the LWTA.xpr
           file, and are documented here through an automatic process which harvests them
           from the xpr file whenever the schema is built.Generally speaking, to use these, you
           select some text in the editor, then press the keystroke shortcut shown in the table
           below. The table uses the following key names:</p>
            <table xml:id="keystrokesTable_ms">
               <row>
                  <cell role="label">M1</cell>
                  <cell role="data">represents the Command key on MacOS X, and the Ctrl key on other platforms.</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell role="label">M2</cell>
                  <cell role="data">represents the Shift key.</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell role="label">M3</cell>
                  <cell role="data">represents the Option key on MacOS X, and the Alt key on other platforms.</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell role="label">M4</cell>
                  <cell role="data">represents the Ctrl key on MacOS X, and is undefined on other platforms.</cell>
               </row>
            </table>
            <table xml:id="codeTemplatesTable">
               <row role="label">
                  <cell>Name</cell>
                  <cell>Description</cell>
                  <cell>Result</cell>
                  <cell>Keystroke</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Escape XML</cell>
                  <cell>Escape a block of XML code in e.g. a pre element</cell>
                  <cell>${xpath_eval(replace('${selection}', '&amp;lt;', '&amp;amp;lt;'))}</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> 7</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert a code element</cell>
                  <cell>Insert an HTML code element</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;code&gt;${selection}${caret}&lt;/code&gt;</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> C</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert a curly apostrophe</cell>
                  <cell>Insert a curly apostrophe</cell>
                  <cell style="font-size: 300%; padding-left: 2em; font-family: 'Noto Sans'">’</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> QUOTE</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert a pre element</cell>
                  <cell>Insert an HTML pre element for plain text</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;pre&gt;${selection}${caret}&lt;/pre&gt;</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M3">M3</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> P</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert a section element</cell>
                  <cell>Insert a new section</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;section&gt;${selection}${caret}&lt;/section&gt;</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> S</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert an ellipsis</cell>
                  <cell>Type the ellipsis character (U+2026, preferred over three dots)</cell>
                  <cell style="font-size: 300%; padding-left: 2em; font-family: 'Noto Sans'">…</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> PERIOD</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert an em element</cell>
                  <cell>Insert an HTML emphasis (em) element</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;em&gt;${selection}${caret}&lt;/em&gt;</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> I</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert an h3 (section heading)</cell>
                  <cell>Insert an h3 element, which is the heading for a section</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;h3&gt;${selection}${caret}&lt;/h3&gt;</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> H</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert an XML/HTML attribute</cell>
                  <cell>Prompted for the name of an attribute, insert an appropriately-escaped code block.</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;code&gt;@${ask('Attribute name?', string, 'attribute')}&lt;/code&gt;</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M3">M3</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> A</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert an XML/HTML element</cell>
                  <cell>Prompted for the name of an element, insert an appropriately-escaped code block.</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;${ask('Element name?', string, '${selection}')}&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;${caret}</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M3">M3</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> E</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert blockquote element</cell>
                  <cell>Insert a blockquote element</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;blockquote&gt; ${selection}${caret} &lt;/blockquote&gt;</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> B</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert li element</cell>
                  <cell>Insert a list item</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;li&gt;${selection}${caret}&lt;/li&gt;</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> L</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert link</cell>
                  <cell>Insert an HTML anchor element</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;a href="${caret}"&gt;${selection}&lt;/a&gt;</cell>
