                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> A</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert ol element</cell>
                  <cell>Insert an ordered list element</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;ol&gt;${selection}${caret}&lt;/ol&gt;</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> O</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert p element</cell>
                  <cell>Insert a paragraph element</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;p&gt;${selection}${caret}&lt;/p&gt;</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> P</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert q element</cell>
                  <cell>Wrap selected text in a q element</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;q&gt;${selection}${caret}&lt;/q&gt;</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> Q</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Insert ul element</cell>
                  <cell>Insert an unordered list element</cell>
                  <cell>&lt;ul&gt;${caret}&lt;/ul&gt;</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M3">M3</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> U</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>Today's date in ISO</cell>
                  <cell>Adds today's date in ISO format (yyyy-mm-dd)</cell>
                  <cell>${date(yyyy-MM-dd)}</cell>
                  <cell>
                     <seg type="key_M1">M1</seg>
                     <seg type="key_M2">M2</seg> D</cell>
               </row>
            </table>
         </div>-->
         <div xml:id="staticSearch">
            <head>The staticSearch functionality</head>
            <p>Because there are two distinct sites, one private and one public, we have two 
               distinct search instances; each site gets its own search page with its own index,
               so that search cannot be used on the public site to discover content which is 
               in the private site.
            </p>
            <p>This project uses the <ref target="https://endings.uvic.ca">Endings Project</ref>'s 
               <ref target="https://github.com/projectEndings/staticSearch">staticSearch</ref> utility to build a completely
                static JavaScript-based search engine for the site. The repository contains a complete static copy of the staticSearch
                codebase in the <ident>staticSearch</ident> folder. This is normally drawn from a release branch of staticSearch; the branch
                is specified in a property called <ident>staticSearchBranch</ident> in the 
                <ident>build.xml</ident> file. Since
                there are occasional updates to release versions of staticSearch, someone should
                periodically run the task to update that codebase. The command would be:
                <eg>ant refreshStaticSearchCode</eg>
            </p>
         </div>
         <!-- DONE TO HERE. -->
         <div xml:id="doStuff">
            <head>How to do stuff</head>
            
            <div xml:id="openOxygenProject">
               <head>How to open the Oxygen project</head>
               <p>All editing should be done with the 
                  <ref target="https://www.oxygenxml.com/download.html">Oxygen XML Editor</ref>. 
               Start Oxygen, then click on <ident>Project</ident> / <ident>Open Project</ident>, 
               browse to the project folder, and select <ident>lwta.xpr</ident>. When 
               Oxygen asks you if you want to allow it to make changes to the Oxygen interface,
               say OK.</p>
            </div>
            <div xml:id="editAFile">
               <head>How to edit an existing file</head>
               <p>All existing site content is stored in the <ident>new/content</ident>
               folder. Open a file in Oxygen and edit it. Before you commit changes 
               back to the Git repository, make sure the file is <emph>valid</emph>
               by clicking on the Red Check icon.</p>
            </div>
            <div xml:id="createAFile">
               <head>How to create a new file</head>
               <p>If you want to add a new page, do this:
               [TODO]
               </p>
               
            </div>
            
            <div xml:id="uploadToServer">
               <head>How to upload a new version of the site to the server</head>
               <p>To do this, you will need to be on a computer which has 
                  <ident>Java</ident>, <ident>Ant</ident> and <ident>rsync</ident> installed.
               Open a terminal in the root folder of the project, and type:</p>
               <p>
                  <eg>ant lwtaRsyncToDevServer</eg>
               </p>
               <p/>
               <p>
                  <eg>ant lwtaRsyncToLiveServer</eg>
               </p>
               <p>You will need to supply the password for the site, which is on the 
               HCMC's nfs system. Note that the live server command is slightly unexpected
               on purpose; this is to prevent a problem which has happened in the past, where
               someone has typed a generic command to publish a site into the wrong command
               terminal, and accidentally published the wrong site. To prevent this, we 
               prefix all live-site publication target names with something unique to the
               project itself.</p>
            </div>
         </div>
         <div xml:id="taggingGuidelines">
            <head>Guidelines for editing and tagging</head>
            <p>All tagging in articles is done using a very constrained XHTML5 schema, and 
                all files must validate according to the W3C’s VNU validator. If 
            you find that there are HTML5 tags or attributes that are missing from 
            our very tight schema and would be useful, just ask @mholmes to add them
            to the ODD file, or do that for yourself and rebuild the schema.</p>
            
         </div>
         <div xml:id="oddAndDocumentation">
            <head>The ODD file and documentation</head>
            <p>The two schemas (RelaxNG and Schematron) that we use to validate and constrain
            the content documents are both generated from the file <ident>schema/LWTA.odd</ident>,
               as is the documentation in <ident>documentation/LWTA.html</ident>. 
               <ref target="http://www.tei-c.org/Guidelines/Customization/odds.xml">ODD files</ref> 
               are normally used to create schemas for TEI XML projects, but this project makes
            use of the ODD specification and processing provided by the TEI infrastructure to 
            provide validation and documentation for documents which are not TEI at all; they're
            pure XHTML5. </p>
            <p>
               <q>Why not just use the standard HTML5 validator?</q> Well, we do, in fact; the 
            output pages in the site are all validated using the <ident>vnu.jar</ident> validator 
            at the end of the build process. However, that validator allows the full range of 
            HTML5 elements and attributes, and it does not constrain the values of important 
            attributes; in other words, it's too permissive. Our own schema is intended to provide 
            much tighter control over what is allowed in the documents in the <ident>posts</ident>
              and <ident>pages</ident>
            directories. This enables us to enforce site-wide styles, and provide more prompts and 
            help for editors working in the Oxygen XML Editor.</p>
         </div>
         <div xml:id="gettingHelp">
            <head>Getting help</head>
            <p>If you need technical help with any aspect of this project/website, 
               contact Martin Holmes <ref target="mailto:mholmes@uvic.ca">mholmes@uvic.ca</ref>.</p>
         </div>
      </body>
      <back>
         <div>
           <!-- We allow multiple starting elements for our schema so that we can 
                validate articles and page-component fragments in their own 
                discrete files, while also validating full pages created from them. -->
            <schemaSpec ident="LWTA"
                        prefix="xh_"
                        start="html head article header footer nav aside main"
                        ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
               <moduleRef key="tei"/>
               <moduleSpec ident="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Base schema module for all XHTML5 elements defined in this ODD.</desc>
               </moduleSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="html" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>The root html element</gloss>
                  <desc>The html element should only appear in templates and completed pages.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="att.identifiable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <sequence>
                        <elementRef key="head"/>
                        <elementRef key="body"/>
                     </sequence>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="head" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>The page head (metadata) element</gloss>
                  <desc>The head element should only appear in templates and completed pages.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <sequence>
                        <elementRef key="title" maxOccurs="1"/>
                        <elementRef key="meta" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                        <elementRef key="link" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                        <elementRef key="script" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                     </sequence>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="title" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <content>
                     <textNode/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="meta" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <content>
                     <empty/>
                  </content>
                  <attList>
                     <attDef ident="name" usage="opt">
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef key="teidata.text"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                     <attDef ident="content" usage="opt">
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef key="teidata.text"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                     <attDef ident="charset" usage="opt">
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef key="teidata.text"/>
                        </datatype>
                        <valList type="closed">
                           <valItem ident="utf-8">
                              <gloss>UTF-8</gloss>
                              <desc>Per the specification, utf-8 is the only acceptable value.</desc>
                           </valItem>
                        </valList>
                     </attDef>
                  </attList>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="body" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>The body element. </gloss>
                  <desc>This has a very constrained content model. It may contain header, article or main, then footer.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <sequence>
                        <elementRef key="header" maxOccurs="1"/>
                        <alternate maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0">
                           <elementRef key="main"/>
                           <elementRef key="article"/>
                        </alternate>
                        <elementRef key="footer"/>
                     </sequence>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="header" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>The page header, containing the site title and other banner info</gloss>
                  <desc>We constrain this severely.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <sequence>
                        <elementRef key="h1"/>
                        <elementRef key="nav"/>
                     </sequence>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="footer" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>The page footer, containing the svn build info and other info.</gloss>
                  <desc>We constrain this severely.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <elementRef key="div" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="div" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>A division of the footer element or the search page.</gloss>
                  <desc>The div is only used in the footer and in the search page right now.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="att.identifiable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.hasLang"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
                        <elementRef key="p"/>
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="main" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>The main element, containing block content</gloss>
                  <desc>This is used only in pages which aren't articles, such as 
                  generated listings pages.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="att.visibility"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.identifiable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <sequence>
                        <elementRef key="h2"/>
                        <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                           <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                              <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                              <elementRef key="br"/>
                           </alternate>
                           <elementRef key="div"/>
                        </alternate>
                        <!-- We allow script here for staticSearch overrides. -->
                        <elementRef key="script" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                     </sequence>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="article" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>The main wrapper for a post; used as the root for post files.</gloss>
                  <desc>An article starts with a heading, and may then have direct content
                  from the lwtablockContent macro, or it may have a series of one or more 
                  section elements.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.identifiable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <sequence>
                        <elementRef key="h2" maxOccurs="1"/>
                        <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
                           <macroRef key="macro.lwtaBlockContent"/>
                           <elementRef key="section" minOccurs="2" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                        </alternate>
                     </sequence>
                  </content>
                  
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="section" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>A subsection in a post</gloss>
                  <desc>If using sections, there must be at least two, and they can 
                  be the only child.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.identifiable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.hasLang"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <sequence>
                        <elementRef key="h3" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1"/>
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaBlockContent"/>
                     </sequence>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="h1" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>Site heading/title</gloss>
                  <desc>The h1 (level 1 heading) element provides the heading for 
                  the entire site. It should only appear inside the <gi>header</gi> element.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                        <elementRef key="br"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="h2" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>Article  heading</gloss>
                  <desc>The h2 (level 2 heading) element provides the heading for 
                  article elements.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockHeading"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                        <elementRef key="br"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="h3" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>Section heading</gloss>
                  <desc>The h3 (level 3 heading) element provides the heading for 
                  sections (if any) in articles.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockHeading"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.identifiable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                        <elementRef key="br"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="h4" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>Section heading</gloss>
                  <desc>The h4 (level 4 heading) element provides the heading for 
                        sub-sections (if any) in articles.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockHeading"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                        <elementRef key="br"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="p" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Prose paragraph.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockBody"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.identifiable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.hasLang"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                        <elementRef key="br"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="details" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Expandable details element with summary child.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockBody"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.identifiable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <sequence>
                        <elementRef key="summary"/>
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaBlockContent"/>
                     </sequence>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="summary" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Single-line summary for details element.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaPhrase"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="blockquote"
                            ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
                            module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Block quotation.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockBody"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.hasLang"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <elementRef key="p"/>
                        <elementRef key="ul"/>
                        <elementRef key="br"/>
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="q" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Inline quotation. In rendering, quotation marks will be supplied, so do not
                     include them.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaPhrase"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <elementRef key="br"/>
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="s" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Text with line through (strikethrough). Signifies deleted text.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaPhrase"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <elementRef key="br"/>
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="nav" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Navigation menu. Should contain a ul element with the menu items as li children.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <elementRef key="ul" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1"/>
                  </content>
                  <attList>
                     <attDef ident="class" mode="replace" usage="req">
                        <valList type="closed">
                           <valItem ident="mainMenu">
                              <gloss>The main site menu</gloss>
                           </valItem>
                        </valList>
                     </attDef>
                  </attList>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="ul" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Unordered list, usually bulleted.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockBody"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.hasLang"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <elementRef key="li" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="ol" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Ordered list, usually numbered.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockBody"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.hasLang"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <elementRef key="li" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="li" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Item in a list or a menu.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.identifiable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <elementRef key="ul"/>
                        <elementRef key="ol"/>
                        <elementRef key="p"/>
                        <elementRef key="pre"/>
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                        <elementRef key="br"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="pre" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Preformatted text which is to be presented exactly as written in the HTML file.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.identifiable"/>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockBody"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.hasLang"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <textNode/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="span" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>General-purpose phrase-level element. Use only if there is no more specific
                     alternative for what you want.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaPhrase"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.hasLang"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                        <elementRef key="br"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
                  <!-- NOTE: Leaving this in place, but we expect this to be 
                   changed or expanded. -->
                  <constraintSpec ident="spansMustHaveStyleOrClass" scheme="schematron">
                     <constraint>
                        <sch:rule context="xh:span">
                           <sch:assert test="@class or @style or @lang"> 
                           A span element must have either @style, @class, or @lang.
                        </sch:assert>
                        </sch:rule>
                     </constraint>
                  </constraintSpec>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="strong" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>Strong text</gloss>
                  <desc>Text that needs to be highlighted because it is important; will be rendered by
                     default in bold.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaPhrase"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="code" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>Inline computer code, filenames etc.</gloss>
                  <desc>Inline text which is computer code or similar text such as identifiers.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaPhrase"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="script" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>Element to contain or link to JavaScript.</gloss>
                  <desc>script element; used only in the search page and the boilerplate in the header, but
                      can also appear in post body content without @src.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockBody"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <textNode/>
                  </content>
                  <attList>
                     <attDef ident="src" usage="opt">
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef key="teidata.pointer"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                  </attList>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="link" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>Element to link to a CSS file or a favicon</gloss>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="att.href"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <empty/>
                  </content>
                  <attList>
                     <attDef ident="rel" usage="req">
                        <gloss>Relation to main file</gloss>
                        <valList type="closed">
                           <valItem ident="stylesheet">
                              <gloss>The <att>href</att> attribute points to a CSS stylesheet.</gloss>
                           </valItem>
                           <valItem ident="icon">
                              <gloss>The <att>href</att> attribute points to a favicon.</gloss>
                           </valItem>
                        </valList>
                     </attDef>
                     <attDef ident="type" usage="opt">
                        <gloss>The type of item pointed to by the link</gloss>
                        <valList type="closed">
                           <valItem ident="image/svg+xml">
                              <gloss>A favicon in SVG format.</gloss>
                           </valItem>
                        </valList>
                     </attDef>
                  </attList>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="style" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>style element; used only in the search page.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <textNode/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="img" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Image element. May be rendered inline or as a block, depending on where it
                     appears in the document structure.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaPhrase"/>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockBody"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.identifiable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <constraintSpec ident="imgWithoutCaptionNeedsAltAndTitle" scheme="schematron">
                     <constraint>
                        <!--<sch:ns uri="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" prefix="xh"/>-->
                        <sch:rule context="xh:img">
                           <sch:assert test="(@alt and @title) or following-sibling::xh:figcaption or ancestor::xh:ul[@class='gallery']"> 
                           If your img element is not inside a figure element with a figcaption, 
                           then it requires @alt and @title attributes to provide help for 
                           visually-impaired users.
                        </sch:assert>
                        </sch:rule>
                     </constraint>
                  </constraintSpec>
                  <attList>
                     <attDef ident="width" usage="opt">
                        <desc>Width in pixels of the image.</desc>
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef key="teidata.numeric"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                     <attDef ident="height" usage="opt">
                        <desc>Height in pixels of the image</desc>
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef key="teidata.numeric"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                     <attDef ident="src" usage="req">
                        <gloss>path to the image (usually a relative path)</gloss>
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef key="teidata.pointer"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                     <attDef ident="alt" usage="opt">
                        <gloss>description of the image for visually-impaired users. If not supplied,
                        then figcaption will be used instead.</gloss>
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef key="teidata.text"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                     <attDef ident="title" usage="opt">
                        <gloss>description of the image which will pop up on mouseover. If not supplied,
                           then figcaption will be used instead.</gloss>
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef key="teidata.text"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                  </attList>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="em" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Emphasized text; will be rendered by default in italics.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaPhrase"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                        <elementRef key="br"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="a" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaPhrase"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.href"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.hasLang"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                  </content>
                  <attList>
                     <attDef ident="title" usage="opt">
                        <gloss>explanation of what is being linked to. Will pop up when
                        mousing over the link.</gloss>
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef key="teidata.text"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                     <attDef ident="target" usage="opt">
                        <valList type="closed">
                           <valItem ident="_blank">
                              <gloss>Open this link in a new window or tab.</gloss>
                           </valItem>
                        </valList>
                     </attDef>
                  </attList>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="figure" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>A figure consists of an image and a caption.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockBody"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.identifiable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <sequence>
                        <elementRef key="img"/>
                        <elementRef key="figcaption" minOccurs="0"/>
                     </sequence>
                  </content>
                  <attList>
                     <attDef ident="class" mode="change" usage="req">
                        <valList type="closed" mode="add">
                           <valItem ident="leftFloat">
                              <gloss>Float this figure to the left and flow the text around it.</gloss>
                           </valItem>
                           <valItem ident="center">
                              <gloss>Centre this figure and do not float text around it.</gloss>
                           </valItem>
                           <valItem ident="rightFloat">
                              <gloss>Float this figure to the right and flow the text around it.</gloss>
                           </valItem>
                        </valList>
                     </attDef>
                  </attList>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="br" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>A hard-coded linebreak. Avoid unless you absolutely need it. Use it at the 
                  end of lines in poems.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <empty/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="figcaption"
                            ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
                            module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Caption for an image in a figure element.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaPhrase"/>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="td" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>A table data cell.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="th" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>A table label or heading cell.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                  </content>
                  <attList>
                     <attDef ident="scope" usage="opt">
                        <valList type="closed">
                           <valItem ident="col">
                              <gloss>Scope of this heading is the column below it.</gloss>
                           </valItem>
                           <valItem ident="row">
                              <gloss>Scope of this heading is the row to the right of it.</gloss>
                           </valItem>
                        </valList>
                     </attDef>
                  </attList>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="tr" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>A table row.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <sequence minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <elementRef key="th" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                        <elementRef key="td" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                     </sequence>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="caption" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>A table caption.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <macroRef key="macro.lwtaParaContent"/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="table" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>A table.</desc>
                  <classes>
                     <memberOf key="att.classable"/>
                     <memberOf key="model.lwtaBlockBody"/>
                  </classes>
                  <content>
                     <sequence>
                        <elementRef key="caption" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1"/>
                        <alternate>
                           <sequence>
                              <elementRef key="thead" maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0"/>
                              <elementRef key="tbody" maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="1"/>
                           </sequence>
                           <elementRef key="tr" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                        </alternate>
                     </sequence>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="thead">
                  <desc>The header of a table.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <elementRef key="tr" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1"/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <elementSpec ident="tbody">
                  <desc>The body of a table.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <elementRef key="tr" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                  </content>
               </elementSpec>
               <macroSpec ident="macro.lwtaParaContent" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Content model for paragraph-type containers such as paragraphs, list items, and
                     so on.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                        <textNode/>
                        <classRef key="model.lwtaPhrase"/>
                     </alternate>
                  </content>
               </macroSpec>
               <macroSpec ident="macro.lwtaBlockContent" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Content model for div container.</desc>
                  <content>
                     <sequence>
                        <classRef key="model.lwtaBlockHeading" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                        <classRef key="model.lwtaBlockBody" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
                     </sequence>
                  </content>
               </macroSpec>
               <classSpec type="model" ident="model.lwtaPhrase" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Groups elements which can appear at the phrase level.</desc>
               </classSpec>
               <classSpec type="model" ident="model.lwtaBlockBody" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Groups elements which can appear below the heading in an article or section.</desc>
               </classSpec>
               <classSpec type="atts" ident="att.classable" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Groups elements which can have a class attribute.</desc>
                  <attList>
                     <attDef ident="class" usage="opt">
                        <gloss>The class attribute provides styles through rules in the CSS
                        stylesheet. </gloss>
                        <datatype maxOccurs="unbounded">
                           <dataRef key="teidata.word"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                     <attDef ident="style" usage="opt">
                        <gloss>The style attribute provides one-off style options for specific
                        and unusual cases. Do not use this unless you know that the element
                        you're styling is unlike any other element on the site.</gloss>
                        <datatype maxOccurs="1">
                           <dataRef key="teidata.text"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                  </attList>
               </classSpec>
               <classSpec type="atts" ident="att.identifiable" module="xhtml5">
                  <desc>Groups elements which may have an id attribute.</desc>
                  <attList>
                     <attDef ident="id" usage="opt">
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef name="ID"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                  </attList>
               </classSpec>
               
               
               
               
               <classSpec type="atts" ident="att.href" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>Groups elements which have the @href attribute.</gloss>
                  <attList>
                     <attDef ident="href" usage="req">
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef key="teidata.pointer"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                  </attList>
               </classSpec>
               <classSpec type="atts" ident="att.hasLang" module="xhtml5">
                  <gloss>Groups elements which have the @lang attribute.</gloss>
                  <attList>
                     <attDef ident="lang" usage="opt">
                        <gloss>A language code conforming to BCP 47.</gloss>
                        <datatype>
                           <dataRef key="teidata.language"/>
                        </datatype>
                     </attDef>
                  </attList>
               </classSpec>
               <!--        Global Schematron constraints    -->
               <constraintSpec ident="schVariables" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:ns uri="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" prefix="xh"/>
                     <sch:pattern>
                        <sch:let name="smartDouble" value="'[“”]'"/>
                        <sch:let name="smartSingle" value="'[‘’]'"/>
                        <sch:let name="straightDouble" value="'&#34;'"/>
                        <sch:let name="straightApos" value="''''"/>
                        <sch:let name="straightQuotes"
                                 value="concat('[', $straightDouble, $straightApos, ']')"/>
                     </sch:pattern>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               <constraintSpec ident="noQuotesInText" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:rule context="xh:*[text()][not(ancestor-or-self::xh:script or ancestor-or-self::xh:style or ancestor-or-self::xh:code or ancestor-or-self::xh:pre)]">
                        <sch:assert test="not(text()[matches(., $straightQuotes)])">
                           Do not use straight quotes in text. Use the q or 
                           span elements wherever possible; for apostrophes, 
                           use the smart version (’).
                        </sch:assert>
                     </sch:rule>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               <constraintSpec ident="onlyPermittedImgAttributes" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:rule context="xh:img">
                        <sch:assert test="every $att in @* satisfies local-name($att) = ('src', 'data-lg-version', 'alt', 'title', 'width', 'height', 'id', 'style', 'class')">
                           Only the following attributes are allowed on img: 'src', 'data-lg-version', 'alt', 'title', 'id', 'style', 'class', 'width' and 'height'.
                        </sch:assert>
                     </sch:rule>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               <constraintSpec ident="noBadImageFilenames" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:rule context="xh:img[ancestor::xh:article]">
                        <sch:assert test="matches(@src, '^img:[a-zA-Z0-9/\._\-]+$')">
                           Image file paths must begin with 'img:' and must be well-formed (no spaces or punctuation).
                        </sch:assert>
                     </sch:rule>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               <constraintSpec ident="spacesAfterPeriods" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:rule context="xh:*[not(self::xh:code or self::xh:pre)][text()]">
                        <sch:assert test="not(text()[matches(., '[^\.]\.[A-Z]')])">
                           Don't forget to put a space after every period.
                        </sch:assert>
                     </sch:rule>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               <constraintSpec ident="noSpacesInHrefs" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:rule context="xh:a">
                        <sch:assert test="not(matches(@href, '\s+'))">
                           There should be no spaces in href attributes (links).
                        </sch:assert>
                     </sch:rule>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               <constraintSpec ident="noLinksInH3s" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:rule context="xh:h3">
                        <sch:assert test="not(xh:a[@href])">
                           Don't place links inside h3 elements.
                        </sch:assert>
                     </sch:rule>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               <constraintSpec ident="noLinksInLinks" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:rule context="xh:a">
                        <sch:assert test="not(descendant::xh:a[@href])">
                           Don't place links inside other links.
                        </sch:assert>
                     </sch:rule>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               <constraintSpec ident="periodsAndCommasInsideQuotes" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:rule context="xh:span[@class=('poemTitle', 'articleTitle', 'artTitle')][not(matches(., '[!\?]$'))]">
                        <sch:assert test="not(following-sibling::node()[1][matches(., '^[\.,]')])">
                           Periods and commas belong inside the span element for a poem title
                           or an article title, because the poem or article title will be 
                           rendered with quotation marks.
                        </sch:assert>
                     </sch:rule>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               <constraintSpec ident="periodsAndCommasOutsideLinks" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:rule context="xh:a[@href]">
                        <sch:assert test="not(matches(., '[\.,:;]\s*$')) or matches(., '((Esq\.)|(A\.\s*W\.)|(\.\s*\.\s*\.))$')">
                           Don't include trailing periods and commas inside link text.
                        </sch:assert>
                     </sch:rule>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               <constraintSpec ident="noLinksInHeadings" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:rule context="xh:h2">
                        <sch:assert test="not(descendant::xh:a)">
                                Don't include links in headings which themselves will become links.
                            </sch:assert>
                     </sch:rule>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               <!-- Excessive style constraint? -->
               <constraintSpec ident="useProperEllipsis" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:rule context="xh:*[not(self::xh:code or self::xh:pre)][text()]">
                        <sch:assert test="not(text()[matches(., '\.\.\.')])">
                           Use an ellipsis (…) rather than three periods.
                        </sch:assert>
                     </sch:rule>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               
               <constraintSpec ident="dateMustMakeSense" scheme="schematron">
                  <constraint>
                     <sch:rule context="xh:article[@data-date]">
                        <sch:assert test="matches(@data-date, '^\d\d\d\d(-\d\d(-\d\d)?)?(/\d\d\d\d(-\d\d(-\d\d)?)?)?$')">
                                The @data-date element must match a single ISO date:
                                yyyy-mm-dd, or yyyy-mm, or yyyy
                                or a single ISO date followed by a slash followed by 
                                a second ISO date:
                                2022-06-01/2022-06-03
                                indicating a date-range.
                            </sch:assert>
                     </sch:rule>
                  </constraint>
               </constraintSpec>
               
            </schemaSpec>
         </div>
      </back>
   </text>
</TEI>
